# ===========================================================================
# Proposal 01 — DanglingReference: storage-description seeAlso → retired
# containers wiki/pages/ + wiki/sources/ (both 404 after the D98 rename).
# Covers pod-audit findings:
#   - resolve:seeAlso @ https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/wiki/pages/
#   - resolve:seeAlso @ https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/wiki/sources/
# ===========================================================================

<urn:uuid:7c1a0d20-5e44-4f3b-9a01-2026052301>
    a as:Announce, mem:RealignAction, prov:Activity ;
    as:actor <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    as:target </vault/wiki/working/curator-proposals/> ;
    as:object </vault/.well-known/solid> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    prov:used </vault/settings/publicTypeIndex> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom </vault/.well-known/solid> ;
    mem:stalenessClass mem:DanglingReference ;
    mem:rationale """The storage description (.well-known/solid) lists rdfs:seeAlso </wiki/pages/> and
</wiki/sources/>. Both return 404. Probed the live container set: wiki/concepts/, wiki/people/,
wiki/places/, wiki/events/, wiki/organizations/, wiki/procedures/, wiki/working/ all return 200;
pages/ and sources/ are gone. The Type Index (prov:used, operational ground truth) confirms the
D98 rename: skos:Concept AND wiki:Source both route to </wiki/concepts/> (reg0/reg1), i.e. the old
pages+sources containers were merged into concepts/. Ground-truth precedence: deployed Pod (live
containers + Type Index) over the static config that still names the retired pair.

ROOT CAUSE (repo-side, NOT HTTP-PATCHable): the storage description is assembled from BOTH
css/config/void-description.json (static StaticStorageDescriber terms) AND
overlays/wiki-memory/storage-patch.ttl (runtime overlay). The overlay storage-patch already emits
the correct D98 set (concepts/ + the five others). The static config still emits the stale
pages/ + sources/ terms, and the merged result is the union — so the stale pair survives every
`make reset`. Repair the static config toward the decision; do not PATCH .well-known/solid (405 /
static). After the repair the merged seeAlso equals the overlay's correct set.""" ;
    as:published "2026-05-23T22:34:12Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

# --- Proposed change (REPO-SIDE, not an N3 Patch) -------------------------
# File: cogitarelink-solid/css/config/void-description.json
# Remove the two StaticStorageDescriber blocks that emit the retired containers:
#
#   - lines ~210-219  { "comment": "L3: wiki pages container (D76)",   ... seeAlso .../wiki/pages/ }
#   - lines ~220-229  { "comment": "L3: wiki sources container (D76)", ... seeAlso .../wiki/sources/ }
#
# Rationale for delete-not-rename: the overlay storage-patch.ttl already supplies the full live
# D98 seeAlso set (concepts/, people/, places/, events/, organizations/, procedures/, working/),
# so the static config does not need to re-emit concepts/. Deleting the two stale blocks is
# sufficient and avoids a duplicate concepts/ term.
#
# After edit + `make reset`, verify:
#   curl -s https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/.well-known/solid | grep seeAlso
#   → must NOT contain wiki/pages/ or wiki/sources/; must list concepts/ (from the overlay).
#
# SECONDARY (AUDITOR-GAP — pod-audit cross-checks rdfs:seeAlso but NOT prof:hasResource).
# Walked the whole storage description per skill guidance. It carries six prof:hasResource targets;
# probed each:
#   meta/profiles/page      -> 200   (load-bearing ROOT profile — do NOT touch; false-positive guard)
#   meta/profiles/concept   -> 200   OK
#   meta/profiles/person    -> 200   OK
#   meta/profiles/working   -> 200   OK
#   meta/profiles/source    -> 404   DANGLING  (mirrors the D98 source→concept rename)
#   meta/profiles/procedure -> 404   DANGLING  (procedure→howto rename; profile never re-emitted)
#
# These two 404s are the SAME class (mem:DanglingReference) the auditor caught on seeAlso, missed
# here because its cross-check set does not yet include prof:hasResource. They live in the SAME
# static config (css/config/void-description.json, the "PROF: ... profile descriptor (D86)" blocks).
# RECOMMENDATION for human review:
#   - profiles/source: the source profile folded into concept (D98). Either point hasResource at
#     </vault/meta/profiles/concept> or drop the source profile term. Confirm against the concept
#     profile's prof:isTransitiveProfileOf chain before choosing.
#   - profiles/procedure: procedure→howto (D98). Verify whether </vault/meta/profiles/howto> exists
#     and re-point, or drop the term.
# Not auto-proposed as separate RealignActions because the correct target (re-point vs drop) needs
# the profile-inheritance chain confirmed — a judgment call for the reviewer. Also: AUDITOR FIX —
# extend pod_audit.py's resolve cross-check to dereference prof:hasResource targets, not just seeAlso.
